From 7ef2d13fbc549dc66857bf2fdb32779cdfa248ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:13:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/71] feat(health): report per-backend and server memory in
 /v1/health

Each all_models_loaded entry with a live pid now carries rss_mib (VmRSS)
and anon_mib (RssAnon) read from /proc/<pid>/status, and a new top-level
server_process object reports lemond's own pid and memory. Values are
MiB rounded to one decimal, Linux-only, and omitted when unreadable.
The /proc reads run in the health handler after the router lock is
released, so other get_all_loaded_models() callers are unaffected.

Adds a header-only lemon::utils process_memory helper with a cpp-ci
unit test, extends the /health endpoint tests, and documents the fields.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
